# DuckDB patches this fork builds the extension for - ONE PER LINE.
#
# A DuckDB extension loads ONLY under the exact patch it was built against, not
# the minor. Measured: the build for v1.5.3 loaded into a stock v1.5.5 CLI is
# refused outright - "The file was built specifically for DuckDB version
# 'v1.5.3' and can only be loaded with that version of DuckDB". Both are 1.5.x.
#
# So "converge the fleet on one minor" is not a convergence criterion. Either
# every consumer pins one exact patch, or the extension is published per patch.
# This file is the second option: add a patch here and the pipeline builds and
# publishes for it, so consumers keep independent upgrade cadences.
#
# Current consumers and the patch each needs:
#   v1.5.3 - luma-server (bundles duckdb =1.10503.1), teras-ext-pgwire
#   v1.5.5 - the lypto image
#
# Removing a line stops publishing for that patch. Do not remove one while a
# consumer is still pinned to it: they will silently fail to load the extension.
#
# NOT the same file as `.github/duckdb-version` (singular), and both are live:
#   duckdb-version  (singular) - the ONE patch the test workflows check out and
#                                run the suite against (ConfigTests, Catalogs,
#                                MinIO, DeletionVectors, NoInline, Debug).
#   duckdb-versions (plural)   - THIS file: every patch the distribution
#                                pipeline builds and publishes for.
# Keep the singular value present in this list, or the fork would publish only
# patches it never tests.
v1.5.3
v1.5.5
